    "title": "The First Four has arrived: How to watch the start of March Madness",
    "text": "March 17, 2026, 10:55 a.m. MTThe NCAA men’s basketball tournament is officially here, as the First Four in Dayton, Ohio tips off to start the three-week run of this part of March Madness.Everything is winding toward the April 6 national championship game, the 67th game of the tournament. Duke, Arizona, Michigan and Florida are the top seeds as the Florida Gators look to defend their title.What is First Four March Madness?The First Four is four games involving the last four at-large teams and the bottom four conference tournament champions, essentially a play-in to the 64-team field that begins Thursday. The First Four was created in 2011 when the tournament expanded from 64 to 68 teams.Three Texas teams are in the first four, as Texas and SMU were the last two teams in the field, while Prairie View A&M will play-in for a 16 seed.March Madness game schedule todayFirst Four4:40 p.m. MT/5:40 p.m. CT: No. 16 UMBC vs. No. 16 Howard (truTV)7:15 p.m. MT/8:15 p.m. CT: No. 11 Texas vs. No. 11 North Carolina State (truTV)March Madness games on Wednesday4:40 p.m. MT/5:40 p.m. CT: No. 16 Prairie View A&M vs. No. 16 Lehigh (truTV)7:15 p.m. MT/8:15 p.m. CT: No. 11 Miami (Ohio) vs. No. 11 SMU (truTV)How to watch First Four gamesTV schedule: truTVStreaming: Sling TVAll First Four matchups will be nationally broadcast on truTV.NCAA Men's Basketball March Madness 2026 ScheduleHere is the full schedule breakdown for the 2026 men's NCAA Tournament:First Four: Tuesday, March 17 and Wednesday, March 18First round: Thursday, March 19 and Friday, March 20Second round: Saturday, March 21 and Sunday, March 22Sweet 16: Thursday, March 26 and Friday, March 27Elite Eight: Saturday, March 28 and Sunday, March 29Final Four: Saturday, April 4National championship game: Monday, April 6Bret Bloomquist can be reached at bbloomquist@elpasotimes.com; @Bretbloomquist on X.",
